              "text": "To stream the channel formerly known as MSNBC live online, it is important to know about a major update: **MSNBC officially rebranded to MS NOW** (short for *\"My Source for News, Opinion, and the World\"*). This change came after parent company Comcast spun off its cable networks (including MS NOW, CNBC, USA Network, and others) into an independent, publicly traded media company called **Versant**.\n\nBecause of this corporate spin-off, **MS NOW is no longer available on Peacock**. \n\nSince MS NOW is a premium cable channel, there is **no official, permanent 100% free live video stream** available online without a TV provider login. However, there are several legal ways to watch the live stream for free using trials, stream the audio for free, or watch full show segments at no cost:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Free Trials on Live TV Streaming Services\nThe easiest way to get a high-quality, legal live video stream of MS NOW for free is by signing up for a free trial with a digital TV provider. You can cancel before the trial ends to avoid being charged:\n*   **DirecTV Stream:** Typically offers a **5-day free trial**. It includes MS NOW in its base \"Entertainment\" package.\n*   **Fubo:** Generally offers a **7-day free trial**. You can find the channel in its Pro plan.\n*   **YouTube TV:** Often offers a **7- to 14-day free trial**. It carries MS NOW as part of its live channel lineup.\n\n### 2. 100% Free Live Audio Streaming\nIf you want to keep up with live coverage on the go and do not need the video feed, you can stream the entire live broadcast feed in audio format for free:\n*   **TuneIn Radio:** You can stream the MS NOW live audio broadcast 24/7 completely free via the TuneIn app or website.\n*   **The MS NOW App:** The official MS NOW app (available on iOS and Google Play) offers free 24/7 live streaming audio of the broadcast. \n\n### 3. Free Show Segments & Highlights\nIf you want to watch the actual video of your favorite shows\u2014like *The Rachel Maddow Show*, *Morning Joe*, *The Beat with Ari Melber*, or *The Last Word with Lawrence O'Donnell*\u2014without paying for a subscription, you can access individual segments shortly after they air:\n*   **Official YouTube Channel:** The official **MS NOW YouTube channel** uploads nearly all major segments and monologue clips in high definition for free within hours of airing.\n*   **MS NOW App / MS.NOW Website:** You can watch a continuous feed of curated video clips, show highlights, and read written editorial analysis for free without logging in.\n\n### 4. The Budget-Friendly Option (No Contract)\nIf you decide you want a permanent live video feed without a massive cable bill, the most affordable cord-cutting option is **Sling TV**:\n*   **Sling Blue:** This plan includes MS NOW and typically costs $45.99/month. Sling frequently runs promotions offering the first month at a heavily discounted rate.",
